WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.612
Hey, I'm Dreamer, and welcome to the workshop.

4
00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:11.704
This is episode one.

5
00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:14.926
By the end of it you'll know your way around Voyage Studio,

6
00:00:14.926 --> 00:00:18.038
and you'll never lose a night's work to a bad save again.

7
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:23.284
Right up top you've got three tabs, and the one after.

8
00:00:23.284 --> 00:00:25.993
Content is where you build everything.

9
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:29.719
Publish is your world's shop window.

10
00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:34.600
Mods is where you add mods to your world: your own, ones you've bookmarked,

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.441
and Browse mods up top opens Voyage's Discover page to find more.

12
00:00:38.441 --> 00:00:40.569
Nothing changes until you hit Apply.

13
00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.959
And Map is, well, the map.

14
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.532
Down the left is the file tree.

15
00:00:47.532 --> 00:00:50.885
Every part of your world lives in a folder here.

16
00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:53.749
Story, map, characters, items, mechanics.

17
00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.748
Open Characters, then NPCs, then World NPCs, and there's every person in your world.

18
00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.456
Can't find something?

19
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:04.526
Don't go digging.

20
00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:09.123
Type in the search box and Studio finds it for you, wherever it's hiding.

21
00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:15.341
Open Characters, then NPCs, then World NPCs, and click a card.

22
00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.814
It opens as a form.

23
00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:20.672
Name, looks, personality, what they want.

24
00:01:20.672 --> 00:01:25.405
Every box has a little info icon that says what it's for.

25
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.294
Back to World NPCs the same way, and this time hit View JSON.

26
00:01:31.294 --> 00:01:35.124
Same person, same data, written out as the raw file.

27
00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:41.093
This is the bit you can copy and paste, and it's where all my guides tell you to paste things.

28
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.030
So which one do you use?

29
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.815
Both. They're the same file.

30
00:01:45.815 --> 00:01:47.983
The form is safer for small edits.

31
00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:50.023
The JSON is faster for big ones.

32
00:01:50.023 --> 00:01:53.593
Just know Studio remembers whichever view you used last,

33
00:01:53.593 --> 00:01:56.462
so if a file opens looking weird, that's why.

34
00:01:57.867 --> 00:01:59.173
Here's the big one.

35
00:01:59.173 --> 00:02:03.091
Saving. The little arrow next to Save opens your options.

36
00:02:03.533 --> 00:02:07.539
Save Draft keeps your work without touching what players see.

37
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.447
Save and Play saves, then starts a game so you can test it.

38
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.345
And Discard throws away everything since your last save, so mind that one.

39
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:23.220
Open any file, say World NPCs, and look up top.

40
00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.817
It tells you if everything's saved.

41
00:02:26.267 --> 00:02:30.330
And this button here downloads your whole world as one file.

42
00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:31.617
That's your backup.

43
00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.394
Grab one before any big change. Trust me.

44
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.800
So, three rules.

45
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.420
Save your draft often, because players never see a draft until you publish.

46
00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.761
Download a backup before anything big.

47
00:02:43.761 --> 00:02:46.841
And never press Discard unless you really mean it.

48
00:02:48.233 --> 00:02:51.008
Last stop, the Publish tab.

49
00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:56.688
Your cover image, your world's name, and the card description players see,

50
00:02:56.688 --> 00:02:59.941
which tops out at two hundred and sixty characters.

51
00:02:59.941 --> 00:03:04.981
We'll do publishing properly in its own episode, so don't hit publish just yet.

52
00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.363
That's Studio in five minutes.

53
00:03:08.363 --> 00:03:14.687
Next episode, we give your world its voice, and I'll show you what the narrator actually reads.

54
00:03:14.687 --> 00:03:18.081
My worlds and guides are at deaththegrim.github.io.

55
00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:22.481
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

